  "result": "The cause was an off-by-one in the comparison. At `shop/pricing.py:10`, `line_subtotal` checked `line.qty > BULK_THRESHOLD` with the threshold set to 10, so the discount only started at 11 units. The policy says 10 or more.\n\n**Fix:** I changed `>` to `>=`. I also added a test that 9 units still get no discount, so that edge is covered too.\n\n**Tests (`python3 -m unittest`):**\n- **Before the fix:** 1 of 6 tests failed: `test_bulk_discount`. It already expected the discount at exactly 10 units (10 \u00d7 $1.00 \u2212 5% = $9.50, plus $0.78 tax = $10.28). So the test was right and the code was wrong.\n- **After the fix:** all 7 tests pass, including the new one.",
